ipped. I didn't run the type checker, so `tests/typing/typing_edit.py` hasn't been checked.\n\n- **`termui.py`:** I added `import os` and updated both overloads and the implementation to the new `filename` annotation. A single `str` or path is wrapped in a one-item tuple. The docstring has the new sentence and the `versionchanged:: 8.5.0` entry.\n- **`_termui_impl.py`:** `Editor.edit_files` takes `Iterable[str | os.PathLike[str]]`. The spec said to change the body only if it didn't build the command correctly from a path. `Popen` accepts paths at runtime, but concatenating them onto a `list[str]` doesn't type-check. So I convert each one with `os.fspath`.\n- **`CHANGES.md`:** The entry is added at the end of the `Unreleased` list, which in this file is the `Version 8.5.0` section.\n\nThe two new `filename` annotation lines in `termui.py` are over 88 characters. I didn't run the formatter or linter, so I don't know whether they'd be reformatted or flagged.", "ttft_ms": 2306, "type": "result", "duration_ms": 26547, "uuid": "e7e6c54f-a475-463a-863b-f7d17eb05dc7", "ttft_stream_ms": 1883, "time_to_request_ms": 54, "first_content_frame_ms": 1883, "queued_turn_count": 0, "result_index": 0}
